2026-09-22 09:27:45 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\n        You are a workflow assistant. Extract parameters for the intent "select_asset_def_by_reference".\n\n        User message:\n        select this: Justice Alito\'s Single-State Override Test\n\n        Parameter schema for this intent:\n        - "reference": type=string, required=True\n\n        Extraction instructions for this intent:\n        - The "reference" parameter must always be set to the asset\'s "title" field.\n- Never return the idea_id or quote.\n- Use the relevant context block (which lists ideas with idea_id, title, quote)\n  to determine which asset the user is referring to.\n\n\n\nRelevant context:\nasset_definitions:\n  - id: 4a1a5795-0f74-453a-96a8-36d5632f8e82, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Alito\'s Enemy-Funding Test, quote: Suppose there\'s a country that proclaims again and again and again that the United States is its biggest enemy\n  - id: 35c4322a-2ed8-4d48-8806-c883711e221b, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Alito\'s Single-State Override Test, quote: A, thinks Candidate A is an insurrectionist, so\n  - id: 58b16c2d-3f52-4dcc-9160-f6f36f994ca9, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Barrett\'s Impeachment Tension Test, quote: Wouldn\'t that be in some tension with impeachment?\n  - id: 9ac70d60-92f7-41c4-bf2d-93c4597dd69f, idea_id: 23-719, title: Chase\'s Cascade of Nullified Acts, quote: nullify every official act taken not only by this particular judge but by anyone who is an insurrectionist or arguably an insurrectionist under Section\n  - id: eb418bc8-3bd1-4dd3-b27f-8c0c266b837f, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Alito\'s Fifty-State Cascade Test, quote: Could that have a cascading effect, and so the decision by a court in one state\n  - id: 9953c85e-30c2-49b9-9ddc-e73fd56d5109, idea_id: 23-719, title: , quote: \n  - id: e57678f8-2514-4e94-aa86-aea8d9b98428, idea_id: 23-719, title: Murray\'s Two-Record Dilemma Test, quote: which holding was correct and then decide that issue for the country.\n  - id: 339c0fbc-3d30-4dcb-9c32-da465830b5d0, idea_id: 23-719, title: Mitchell\'s Pardon Mechanism Test, quote: Well, we don\'t think it\'s - we don\'t think this problem is fatal because,\n  - id: e0f3a145-40a1-4be8-9067-b3bce18a10c3, idea_id: 23-719, title: Gorsuch Presses Murray on Constitutional Source, quote: Members of this Court have disagreed about that.\n  - id: f2ecf29c-cff1-4407-b263-07e071b313ae, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Jackson Isolates Mitchell\'s Second Argument, quote: But that\'s the second argument. That is. And the - So the first argument - Mm-hmm. -- is we have a list\n  - id: c84a4e7d-6625-459f-9fbb-8c7721fcca38, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Jackson\'s Office Door Test, quote: Yes. But doesn\'t that at least suggest ambiguity?\n  - id: 908f62e2-094e-49f8-9a21-144db1e59295, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Alito\'s Treaty Force Reimagining, quote: we\'re referring to is the proposition that a particular provision of the Constitution or a statute in and of itself creates a private right\n  - id: 89b92e41-15f8-4173-a3bd-313c5010faba, idea_id: 23-719, title: Justice Sotomayor\'s Birthday Ballot Test, quote: can imagine a scenario where the person is 34 years old at the time of the election, but he turns 35 before Inauguration Day.\n  - id: 4d222e76-97e5-4dd0-979d-50b653a6fd6d, idea_id: 23-719, title: Gorsuch Demands Murray Explain the Doctrine\'s Failure, quote: On your theory, would anything compel a - a lower official to obey an order from, in your view, the former president?\n  - id: db8b3243-8370-4d6a-84b6-d7d0f39e3368, idea_id: 23-719, title: , quote: \n  - id: 132eb5ba-bed1-4768-a1fd-40aaa066bada, idea_id: 23-719, title: Gorsuch Tests Disqualification Without Section 3, quote: it without Section 3? Could they disqualify somebody for -- you -- you know, on whatever basis they wanted outside of the Qualifications Clause?\n  - id: 98142f8c-83c8-4c63-9966-732feb55023d, idea_id: 23-719, title: Mitchell Distinguishes Officers from Officeholders, quote: So they\'re officers, but they\'re not offices under the United States because of the Incompatibility Clause,\n  - id: f20bbbfa-5ec1-4373-b851-4e7da9382944, idea_id: 23-719, title: Mitchell Moves Deadline Forward in Time, quote: effectively moving forward in time the deadline that\n  - id: b790d2ec-1541-4351-a3f0-8d8485426003, idea_id: 23-719, title: The Ballot Barrier Paradox, quote: be used to exclude a presidential candidate from the ballot even if that candidate is disqualified from serving as president under Section 3 because\n  - id: f5c81976-a256-450c-a8a6-8a3cdaba18dc, idea_id: 23-719, title: , quote: \n  - id: d8ab3c94-9b22-4d14-a963-15985fa6ef3c, idea_id: 23-719, title: Elected Officials Excluded from Officer Status, quote: officers of -- of the United States are appointed officials, and elected officials,\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
